    "q-257220": {
      "dom_id": "step-q257220",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,2]\\times [-1,3]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={x}^{3}-xy-{y}^{2}+3.\n$$\n\nCalculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization that starts at ${x}_{0}=[2,\\,3]^{T}$ if the first iteration of the algorithm gives ${x}_{1}=[0.96,\\,-0.48]^{T}.$ Round your final answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">${x}_{2}≈[$</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n$-0.221$\n</td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}-xy-{y}^{2}+3) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}-xy-{y}^{2}+3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-y \\\\ -x-2y\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}-y) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(-x-2y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}-y) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(-x-2y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6x & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}6x & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-y \\\\ -x-2y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-{[\\begin{aligned}6x & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-y \\\\ -x-2y\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.96 \\\\ -0.48\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}6(0.96) & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3(0.96)^{2}-(-0.48) \\\\ -0.96-2(-0.48)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.96 \\\\ -0.48\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}5.76 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3.2448 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.96 \\\\ -0.48\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{5.76\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5.76\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3.2448 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.96 \\\\ -0.48\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{12.52}[\\begin{aligned}-6.4896 \\\\ 3.2448\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}0.442 \\\\ -0.221\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
